  "unJoueurEstDesigneComme": "A player is designated as a ''target''. The other players anonymously answer a question about them. The target chooses their preferred answer, and the author of that answer earns one point.",
  "uneSituationEstPresenteeTous": ": \r\n        \"A situation is presented. All players vote for the person most likely to do this thing. The player who receives the most votes earns one point (a dubious honor!).\",    ",
  "modeClassiqueUneQuestionEst": "Classic Mode: A question is asked. One player is secretly designated as a ''liar'' and must invent an answer. The others tell the truth. Vote to unmask the liar.\\n\\nSimplified Mode: Everyone tells an anecdote (true or false) in response to a theme, then secretly declares their truthfulness. Then, everyone votes ''True'' or ''False'' for each story. You earn points by guessing correctly and deceiving others.",
  "laPlupartDesJoueursCivils": "Most players (Civilians) will receive a word. An ''Infiltrator'' receives a similar word. And a ''Mr. White'' receives NO word. Each player receives a clue word in **30 seconds**. The goal is to unmask the impostors by voting. If a civilian is eliminated, the impostors win.",
  "unMotEstAfficheChaque": "A word is displayed. Each player must secretly submit a synonym. All answers are revealed, and then players vote to ''ban'' the least relevant proposition. The banned player loses the round.",
  "plusieursCategoriesSontSelectionnees3": "Several categories are selected (3 minimum). A category is displayed (e.g. Car make). Each player in turn must write a valid word (e.g. Volvo, Citroën) before the end of his timer. If a player does not answer in time, he wins 1 point. The player with the fewest points wins.",
  "uneQuestionSecreteEstAffichee": "A secret question is displayed. The designated player chooses ''Tails'' or ''Heads''. If their choice is incorrect, they must reveal the question and answer it honestly.",
  "leJoueurDesigneDoitRepondre": "The designated player must answer a difficult dilemma. There is no right or wrong answer, just difficult choices!",
  "deuxEquipesSaffrontentChaqueEquipe": "Two teams compete against each other. Each team must find all its words out of 25, thanks to the clues given by its spymaster. Warning: a word \"assassinâ€Â€\" makes you lose immediately! In local mode, the spymaster looks at the map on the screen and guides his team. In multiplayer, the game manages the roles and the key card.",
  "faireDevinerUnMaximumDe": "Make as many cards as possible guess in 3 rounds (free description, one word, mime), with fewer and fewer clues. The team with the most points wins. In local mode, the phone goes from player to player for guessing. In multiplayer, the game manages roles, laps and the timer.",
  "passezLeTelephoneDeMain": "Pass the phone from hand to hand as quickly as possible. When the music or the clock stops, the person with the phone has to answer a funny or spicy question. Great for breaking the ice!",
  "unJoueurTientLeTelephone": "One player holds the phone to their forehead. The others describe the word displayed. Tilt the phone down to ''guess'', up to ''pass''.",
  "trouvezDesMotsCorrespondantA": "Find words that fit into given categories, starting with a specific letter. Score points for unique and correct answers.",
  "chaqueJoueurRecoitLeMeme": "Each player receives the same meme. He must add the funniest description. Then, all the descriptions are revealed to the other players who vote for the funniest one. The author of the description that receives the most votes earns one point.",
  "vaincreLesVillageoisEstSon": "Defeating the villagers is his goal. During the night he wakes up with the other werewolves. Once in the game, he can change their victim into a werewolf. The infected player retains his role and powers, and accumulates the properties of a Werewolf: he wakes up at night with the wolves to vote, and wins the game by eliminating all the innocents. The seer cannot know her identity as a Werewolf, which makes the player more difficult to identify and more powerful. Conversely, the Mentalist and the Gravedigger can find the infected thanks to their power.",
  "vaincreLesVillageoisEstSon1": "Defeating the villagers is his goal. Every day, he receives a message telling him a word he must say before sunset, if he wants to stay alive. The Talkative Wolf is therefore a Werewolf with an additional constraint. He dies at the end of the day if he has failed to place his word. He has no words to place when the Dictator takes power, unless power is taken in the second round of the mayoral election. If the Dictator dies at night or in the morning while he had activated his power, the Talkative Wolf has no word!",
  "finirSeulSurvivantEstSon": "Ending up as the sole survivor is his goal, he wakes up at night with the other werewolves who believe he is allied. Every other night, he can devour another player of his choice. Starting on the second night and every other night, the White Wolf has the opportunity to devour a player or a Werewolf during his White Wolf vote (after the witch). The White Wolf''s power is greater than the protective roles. A Protected Guard, or a Red Riding Hood, will be vulnerable to the White Wolf. Even if the White Wolf were to be infected by the Black Wolf, he must win alone. If the White Wolf is in a relationship, he must win with his partner because he can never be the only survivor.",
  "lePremierJourLObjectif": "On the first day, the Mercenary''s objective is to eliminate the target assigned to him. If he succeeds, he wins the game on his own instantly. Otherwise, he becomes a villager. The nickname of the Mercenary''s target is indicated at daybreak. On the first day, the Mercenary has the opportunity to vote at the last second in the event of a tie on his target to influence the vote in his favor and win the game instantly. Even in a couple, the Mercenary has the possibility of winning alone in the first round.",
  "sonObjectifEstDeContaminer": "Its objective is to contaminate all players. Every night, it can contaminate two players. It wins the game when all players are infected with the disease. Contaminated players know the identity of all other contaminated players. The Sick Rat cannot contaminate itself.",
  "sonObjectifEstDeVaincre": "His goal is to defeat the Werewolves. His word is his only power of persuasion to eliminate the Werewolves. In the event of a tie in the daily vote and no mayor is elected, no player dies. The votes of the Ordinary Villagers can be decisive in the fight against the Werewolves.",
  "sonObjectifEstDeVaincre1": "Her goal is to defeat the Werewolves. Each night, she can find out the role of a player she has chosen. She must help the innocent without being unmasked. The Seer cannot detect if a player is infected with the Black Wolf, she only has access to their role. Copying the text indicating the role of the player being observed is considered anti-game.",
  "sonObjectifEstDeVaincre2": "Her goal is to defeat the Werewolves. She wakes up every night and can use one of her two potions: heal the victim of the Werewolves, or kill someone. She only has one copy of each potion. Her death potion overrides the Protection of the Guard or Hunter on Red Riding Hood.",
  "sonObjectifEstDeVaincre3": "Her goal is to defeat the Werewolves. She gets up at night when the Werewolves choose to spy on their exchanges. The Little Girl sees all the messages written by the Wolves at night. However, these are anonymized by a nickname and a random avatar.",
  "sonObjectifEstDeVaincre4": "His goal is to defeat the Werewolves. When the Hunter dies, he has the power to bring another player with him to his grave.",
  "sonObjectifEstDeVaincre5": "His goal is to defeat the Werewolves. Each night, he can protect a different player from an attack by the Werewolves. The Guard cannot protect the same person consecutively. He can protect himself. The protected player remains vulnerable to other attacks such as the Witch''s Death Potion.",
  "sonObjectifEstDeVaincre6": "His objective is to defeat the Werewolves. On the first night, he designates two lovers. If one dies, the other will follow him to his grave. Cupid has the only power to name the two lovers. Once designated, he becomes similar to a Simple Villager. He can designate himself as a lover. The two lovers can belong to different camps. If a Wolf is paired with a Villager, they will then have to eliminate all the players to win the game. The two lovers can chat at any time through a private chat that can be activated via the button to the right of the place where messages are written. The Cupid does not win with the couple but with the village or the wolves if he is infected.",
  "sonObjectifEstDeVaincre7": "His goal is to defeat the Werewolves. He can see the outcome of the village''s vote 30 seconds before it ends. He can determine whether the village''s majority vote targets a Werewolf or not, and influence players to change their vote. Unlike the Seer, he can detect a player infected with the Black Wolf. As a Mentalist, you can''t detect the rat and the infected.",
  "vaincreLesLoupsGarousEst": "Defeating the werewolves is his goal. At night, he can communicate with the dead, in order to extract crucial information...",
  "vaincreLesLoupsGarousEst1": "Defeating the werewolves is his goal. When he dies, the gravedigger digs the grave of a player he chooses and a player from the opposite side. The names of these two players will be announced...",
  "vaincreLesLoupsGarousEst2": "Defeating the werewolves is his goal. He can take over the voting power of the village once in the game. If he executes a werewolf, he becomes Mayor, if not, he dies. After deciding to make a coup, the Dictator takes the vote at daybreak, or after the mayor election on the second day. If the Dictator dies at night or in the morning while activating his power, the Talkative Wolf has no words!",
  "sonObjectifEstDeVaincre8": "His goal is to defeat the Werewolves. As long as the Hunter is alive, he is protected from Werewolf attacks. When the Wolves target Red Riding Hood while the Hunter is alive, their vote does not result in death. If the Hunter dies, then Red Riding Hood becomes similar to a Simple Villager. ",
  "sonObjectifEstDeVaincre9": "His goal is to defeat the Werewolves. Each night, the Pyromancer has the choice of storing a Greek fire barrel at a player''s home, or setting off their explosion. He can kill members of his own side, so he must act strategically. There is no limit to the number of barrels to be placed, but if the Pyromancer dies without triggering an explosion, the players remain alive. Be careful, unlike the Witch, the Pyromancer must be alive in the morning for the explosion to be triggered.",
  "sonObjectifEstDeVaincre10": "His objective is to defeat the Werewolves until he receives a new role. On the first night, he designates a testator who will bequeath his role to him upon his death. The Heir only recovers the powers not consumed by his testator (Witch''s potion, the Dictator''s seizure of power, etc.), except for the Hunter and the Gravedigger. He does not recover the infection (Black Wolf) or the contamination (Sick Rat) from his testator. He keeps the infection or contamination he had at the base. If he inherits the powers of a Werewolf, the other wolves are informed that he is joining the pack. If he inherits the powers of a Dictator who dies on the night of his coup d''état, it will be up to the Heir to assume the consequences and carry out the coup d''état as soon as he wakes up.",
