  "marquesDeVetements": "Clothing markings",
  "butDuJeuEtreLe": "**Game goal**\nBe the player with the most points at the end of the game.\n\n**Draft**\n1. Each player receives **7 response cards** in hand.\n2. A player is named **Juge** (the role turns at each round).\n3. The Judge reads the **question card** aloud.\n4. All **other players** secretly choose **1 reply card** from their hand and submit it.\n5. The judge reads all the answers and designates **the funniest**.\n6. The winner of the round score **1 point**.\n7. Each player **poche** a new card to return to 7.\n8. The role of Judge passes to the next player.\n\n** Important rules**\n- Judge ** doesn''t play** card during his turn.\n- The answers are **anonymous**: the Judge does not know who wrote what.\n- We can only play one card** per handle.",
  "objectifPrenezDesCartesPour": "** Objective**\nTake cards to create matching pairs. Avoid being the player who holds the Zombie card at the end of the game.\n**Draft**\n1. The game starts with 33 cards (16 pairs + 1 Zombie card).\n2. The cards are distributed to the 4 players.\n3. Each turn a player takes a card from the next player.\n4. If the card creates a pair, it is automatically defeated.\n5. The player''s hand is mixed.\n6. The first player to no longer have cards won.\n7. The remaining player with the Zombie card lost!",
  "butDuJeuObtenirLe": "**Game goal**\nGet the highest score by filling 13 categories with 5 dice.\n\n**Running of a tower**\n1. **Lance** : You can throw the 5 dice up to 3 times per turn.\n2. **Keep** : After the 1st or 2nd throw, you can keep some dice and restart others.\n3. **Score**: After at least one throw, you have to choose a category to score. Each category can only be used once per part.\n\n**Category**\n- **As to Six** : Sum of the corresponding dice. (Bound 35 points if the upper section totals 63 points or more).\n- **Brelan** (3 or more identical dice): Sum of all the dice.\n- ** Square** (4 or more identical dice): Sum of all the dice.\n- **Full** (3 dice identical + 1 pair): 25 points.\n- **Small Suite** (4 consecutive dice): 30 points.\n- **Large Suite** (5 consecutive dice): 40 points.\n- **Yams** (5 dice identical): 50 points.\n- **Chance** : Sum of all the dice.",
  "objectifNePasAvoirL": "** Objective**\nDo not have the device in your hands when the potato explodes!\n\n**Draft**\n1. A theme appears on the screen.\n2. The player holding the device must give an answer corresponding to the theme.\n3. As soon as he answered, he quickly passed the plane to his neighbor.\n4. The neighbour must in turn find a new answer and pass the device.\n5. Time is hidden and random: the potato can explode at any time!\n6. The player holding the device at the time of the explosion loses the handle and receives a pledge.",
  "principeGeneralGribouillisEstUn": "**General principle**\nGribouillis is a drawing game inspired by the \"Arab phone\", where ideas change at each stage. There are 3 game modes:\n\n**1. Normal Mode (Arabic Illustrated Phone)**\n- **Writing**: Each player writes a sentence.\n- **Drawing**: Each player receives another sentence and draws it.\n- **Devinette** : Each player receives a drawing and guesses what it represents.\n- **Alternance** : The game alternates drawing and guess until each \"album\" has gone around all the players.\n- **But** : Have fun seeing how a simple sentence turns into something completely different!\n\n**2. Complement Mode (Collaborative Drawing)**\n- **Croquis**: Each player starts a simple drawing.\n- **Complete**: Each player receives another''s drawing and must enrich it, without deleting what already exists.\n- **Alternance**: The drawing goes from player to player, each adding its touch.\n- **Parameter \"Add 1\"**:\n- *If disabled (default)*: It is a string. The drawing evolves at each stage (Player A -> Player B -> Player C...).\n- *If activated*: The initial drawing of each player is completed by all other players, creating several collective works in parallel.\n- **But**: Create surprising and fun collective works of art.\n\n**3. Brise-Glace Mode (Creative Interaction)**\n- **Writing**: Each player writes a personal theme (ex: AppLocalizations.of(context)!.myPreference).\n- **Drawing**: Each player receives the themes from **all other players** and must draw them.\n- **But** : Ideal to break the ice, discover the tastes of others and launch creativity in a collaborative and light way.",
  "yzObjectifAvoirLeMoins": "Objective\n\nHave as few points as possible at the end of the game.\nThe game stops when a player reaches 100 points or more, and the winner is the one with the lowest total score.\n\nEquipment\n\n150 cards numbered from –2 to +12\n\nImplementation\n\nMix all the cards.\nEach player receives 12 cards, placed face down in front of him, in 4 columns × 3 rows.\nThe other cards form a stock. Return the first card to form the waste.\nEach player returns 2 cards of his choice from his 12.\n\nThe course of a tour\n\nIn turn, you have **30 seconds** to choose between two actions:\n\n1. Take the waste card\nYou must exchange it with one of your 12 cards (visible or hidden side).\nThe replaced card goes on the waste.\n\n2. Piocher a card face down\nYou look at the map:\n- either you keep it and replace one of your cards (as above),\n- either you refuse it → you place it directly on the waste, and in this case you must return one of your cards still hidden.\n\nSpecial rules\n\nThree identical cards in a column → are immediately defeated (value 0).\n\nEnd of handle:\n\nThe handle ends when a player has revealed all his cards.\nAll other players then reveal their remaining cards. The handle''s over.\nAll players count the sum of their cards.\n\nPlease note: if the player who finishes does not have the lowest score in the round, he takes a penalty of +10 points (his handle score is doubled in the original version, we will use +10 to simplify).\n\nEnd of game\n\nWe play as many sleeves as we need.\nOnce a player reaches 100 points or more, the game stops.\nThe player with the lowest cumulative score wins.",
  "iAReglesDuPoker": "Objective\n\nWin the chips from other players by having:\n- the best hand of 5 cards during slaughter,\n- or by making them give up (to sleep) thanks to the bets.\n\nHand classification (from strongest to weakest)\n\n1. Royal flush : 10 – V – D – R – A of the same colour\n2. Quint flush: 5 cards that follow each other, same color\n3. Square: 4 identical cards\n4. Full: 3 identical cards + 1 pair\n5. Colour (flush): 5 cards of the same color (non-consecutive)\n6. Next (Fifth): 5 cards that follow each other (different colors)\n7. Brelan: 3 identical cards\n8. Double pair\n9. Pair\n10. High card (highest card if no one gets better)\n\nð\n\n1. Blinds\nThe player to the left of the dealer sets the small blind.\nThe next player sets the big blind.\n\n2. Distribution\nEach player receives 2 closed cards (the \"private cards\").\n\n3. Auction towers and common cards\n- Preflop: bet trick with private cards.\n- Flop: 3 common maps revealed. New bets.\n- Tower: 4th common map revealed. New bets.\n- River: 5th and last common map revealed. Last bet.\n\n4. Shooting (showdown)\nIf several players stay, each shows their game.\nThe best combination of 5 cards (among its 2 private cards + the 5 communes) wins the pot.\n\nPossible actions\n\nIn turn, a player has **30 seconds** for:\n- Checker: don''t bet anything, only if nobody''s ever bet again.\nPut some chips in the pot.\n- Follow (Call): equal the running.\n- Relaunch (Raise): increase the bet.\n- Go to bed (Fold): drop his cards and get out of it.\n\nEnd of game\n\nThe game continues as long as there remain at least 2 players with chips.\nThe final winner is the one who takes all the chips.",
  "butDuJeuGagnerLe": "**Game goal**\nWin the most XP by carrying out actions and responding to truths!\n\n**Draft**\n1. The roulette is the player whose turn it is.\n2. The player shoots \"Action\" or \"Verity\".\n3. Classic mode: A random challenge/question is displayed.\n4. Judge Mode: A random player writes the challenge, then the player realizes it.\n5. Other players validate with a vote Yes/No.\n6. The validation percentage determines the XP won.\n\n**Special rules**\n- 100% validation = maximum XP\n- Player with the most XP becomes Admin of the game\n- The button \"End of handle\" allows to close the part",
  "butDuJeuLeBut": "**Game goal**\nThe goal is to be the first to get rid of all his cards to become President. The last player with cards in hand becomes the Asshole.\n\n**Material and Players**\n- **Maps** : 52 cards.\n- **Players**: 3 to 6 players.\n\n**Card Value**\nThe order of the cards, from the weakest to the strongest, is:\n**3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, Valet, Lady, King, As, 2.**\nThe **2** is the strongest card and can beat any other card or combination.\n\n**Manual operation**\n1. **Distribution**: All cards are distributed equally among players.\n2. **First round**:\n- For the very first game, the player who owns the **3 of Trèfle ( He must play this card (only or with others 3).\n- For the next sleeves, the **Assess wheel** of the previous sleeve starts.\n3. **Play cards**: The first player puts on the table:\n- Only one card (e.g. one 7).\n- One pair (ex: two 8).\n- A brelan (ex: three Valets).\n- One square (ex: four 5).\n4. **Continued from round**: The next player (in a clockwise direction) has **30 seconds** to play the same number of cards** but a **higher value**.\n- Example: If a player poses a pair of 6, the next one must pose a pair of 7, Ladies, As, etc. \n5. **Skip your turn**: If a player cannot or does not want to play, he must pass his turn. Once a player has passed, he cannot play again until the end of the current fold.\n6. **End of a fold**: The fold ends when all players have passed their turn. The last player to have placed cards wins the fold, picks up the cards from the table (set them aside) and starts the next fold by playing what he wants.\n7. **The power of 2**: Play one or more **2** beats any combination and ends the fold instantly. The person who played the 2 wins the fold and starts playing again.\nTo beat a pair, you have to play a pair of 2! \n\n**End of the English Channel and Roles**\n- As soon as a player has no cards, he''s done. The game continues until there is only one player left.\n- The order of the end determines the roles for the next round:\n- **1st**: President\n- **2nd**: Vice-President\n- **Last** : Asshole\n- **Before-last** : Vice-Ass-Trou\n- **Other** (if any): Neutral\n\n**Next month: Card Exchange! **\nBefore starting the new round, players exchange cards:\n- The **Asshole** gives his **two best cards** to the **President**.\n- The **Chair** gives him in return the **two cards of his choice** (usually his worst).\n- If there are 4 players or more, the **Vice-Cut** gives its **best card** to the **Vice-President**.\n- The **Vice-President** gives him the **map of his choice**.\n\n**Special rules**\n- â›â€ **Cannot end with a 2**: A player has no right to get rid of his last card if it is a 2. This blow is considered invalid.\n**Variant Revolution (optional)**: If a player sets a square (4 identical cards), he can announce \"Revolution!\". The order of value of the cards is then reversed until the end of the sleeve (the 3 becomes the strongest, and the 2 the weakest).",
  "butDuJeuReussirDeux": "**Game goal**\nSuccess two challenges before the other players.\n\n**In place**\n- Each player starts with 4 cards: 3 Roses and 1 Skull.\n- Every card on the carpet remains tied to its owner.\n\n**Draft**\n1. In turn, a player can put a card face down on his carpet.\n2. When he no longer wants to pose, he challenges by announcing the number of cards he thinks he can return.\n3. Other players can bid or pass.\n4. The highest bidder becomes the challenger and returns the advertised cards.\n5. First he returns his own cards, then those of other players if necessary.\n\n**Resolution**\n- If a Skull appears, the challenge is lost.\n- If the challenge is won, the player scores a point. The first at 2 points wins the game.\n- If a challenge is lost, the player loses a card at random from his remaining hand. If he loses his Skull, he has to undo another one immediately.",
  "butDuJeuFaireDeviner": "**Game goal**\nTo guess a word by drawing, before the end of the allotted time.\n\n**Draft**\n1. **Drawer/word selection**: A player is designated to draw, and a word is secretly attributed to him.\n2. **Drawing**: The draftsman has a limited time to guess the word by drawing. He can neither speak nor mimic nor write letters or figures.\n3. **Devinettes**: Other players offer words in a chat.\n4. **Validation**: The cartoonist sees the proposals in the chat and clicks on a \"Find!\" button next to the good message to designate the winner.\n5. **Points**: The player who found and the draftsman win a point.\n6. **Next Tower**: A new draftsman is appointed.\n\n**Options**\n- **Only 30 strokes**: The draftsman is limited to a maximum of 30 traits.",
  "butDuJeuFaireDeviner1": "**Game goal**\nLet your partner guess as many mysterious words as possible, each writing a single word clue. The same or invalid indices shall be eliminated.\n\n**Draft**\n1. **Selection of the Devin**: A player is designated as the \"Devin\" for the round. He doesn''t see the word mystery.\n2. **Choice of the Word Mystery**: The Devin chooses a word from a list (or the master of the game chooses one).\n3. **Indice Writing**: All other players (\"Indices\") secretly write ONE single word index that will help the Devin find the word mystery.\n4. **Indices Filter**: All indices are revealed. The same indices (even if spelled differently, e.g. \"chat\" and \"chats\") or invalid (very close to the word mystery, invented, etc.) are eliminated. Only the unique and valid clues are shown in the Devin.\n5. **Devinette** : The Devin looks at the remaining clues and tries to guess the word mystery. He only has one attempt.\n6. **Rating**:\n- If the Devin finds the word mystery: The team wins 1 point.\n- If the Devin doesn''t find the word mystery: 0 point.\n- If the Devin doesn''t answer: 0 point.\n\n**Examples of invalid indices:**\n- Mystery word: \"Chat.\" Invalid indices: \"chaton\", \"feel\", \"miaou\", \"minou\".\n- Identical indices: If 2 players write \"animal\" for \"Chat\", \"animal\" is eliminated.",
  "butDuJeuPourLes": "**Game goal**\n- For **Village**: Eliminate all Wolf-Garous, White Wolf, Malade Rat (except Mercenary if it wins).\n- For the **Loups-Garous** (Loup-Garou, Loup Noir, Loup Bavard): Eliminate all Villagers.\n- For the **Solitaires** : Objective specific to each person (White Loup: being alone; Mercenary: Kill his target at J1; Rat Sick: contaminate all).\n- For the ** Lovers** (if Wolf + Village) : To be the only two survivors.\n\n**Draft**\nThe game alternates between phases of **night** and **day**.\n\n* Night**\n1. The game leader (the app) announces that the village is asleep.\n2. Different characters wake up in turn to use their powers:\n- **Cupidon** (first night only): Names two players who will fall in love. If they are a Wolf and a Villager, their goal changes.\n- The**Heritage** (first night only): Refers to a tester.\n- The **Seeing** wakes up and designates a player to discover his true role. (Do not detect Black Wolf infection).\n- The **Mentalist** (passive) perceives the outcome of the village vote.\n- The **Rat Malade**: Contaminates two players (who will know the others contaminated).\n- The **Loups-Garous** (Loup-Garou, Loup Noir, Loup Bavard - vote together) wake up, concert and designate a victim to eat.\n- The **Black Loup** can once turn the victim into an infected Loup-Garou (who keeps his powers and becomes Wolf). The Mentalist and Fossoyer can detect the infected, the Voyante no.\n- The **White Loup** (one night out of two): Despouses a player of his choice (overturns the protections).\n- Sorcery** wakes up. She sees the wolf victim and can use one of her two potions (only once per part): a potion of **healing** to save the victim, or a potion of**poisoning** to kill someone.\n- The **Pyroman** : Chooses to store a barrel of Greek fire or detonate those already placed (must be alive in the morning).\n- The **Necromancer**: May communicate with the dead.\n\n* Day**\n1. The village is waking up. The app announces who died overnight.\n2. Dead players reveal their role and are eliminated (they can no longer communicate, except the Necromank with the dead).\n- Le **Loup Bavard** : Must utter a secret word or die at sunset (unless Dictator takes power).\n3. Survivors are arguing to try to expose impostors.\n4. After the discussions, all players vote to eliminate a suspect.\n- The **Dictator** (once): Can take the vote. If he eliminates a wolf, he becomes Mayor; Otherwise, he dies.\n- The **Captain** : His vote counts double. If eliminated, he must appoint a successor before he dies.\n- The **Mercenary**: If his target is eliminated on the first day, he wins alone. Otherwise, he becomes a Villager.\n5. The player who receives the most votes is eliminated, reveals his role, and is out of the game.\n- The **Chasseur** : If he is eliminated (day and night), he has the power to bring another player with him.\n- The **Fossoyeur** : When he died, he identified two players (one from the opposite camp, one from his camp).\n- The Lovers**: If one dies, the other follows him with grief.\n- The**Heritage**: If his testator dies, he takes up his role (unless dead or contaminated).\n6. A new night begins.\n\n**Conditions of Victory**\n- **Village**: Eliminate all Wolf-Garous, White Wolf, Sick Rat.\n- **Loups-Garous** (moute): To be equal or higher in number to the Villagers.\n- **White Loup**: Being the only survivor.\n**Mercenary**: Kill his target on the first day.\n- **Rat Malade**: Contaminate all live players.\n- ** Lovers** (Loup + Village) : To be the only two survivors.\n\n**Important notes**\n- The **Chaperon Rouge** is protected by the Hunter against the Wolf-Garous while the Hunter is alive.\n- The **Garde** protects a Wolf-Garous target (cannot protect twice the same person).\n- The White Wolf''s powers don''t know the protections.\n- The Pyroman must be alive in the morning for its barrels to explode.",
